---
description: |
  Builds an OCSF process ancestry from the Kunai `ancestors` of an event.

  Kunai lists the executable paths of the ancestors from the oldest process down
  to the direct parent. OCSF expects the opposite order, so the operator reverses
  the list. Kunai releases up to 0.7.0-rc.1 emit the list as a single string with
  `|` as separator, and the operator reads that form too. The markers `?` and
  `(truncated)` stand for ancestors that Kunai could not resolve and do not
  describe a process, so the operator skips them.
args:
  positional:
    - name: ancestors
      type: field
      description: The Kunai ancestors to consume.
    - name: ancestry
      type: field
      description: The field that receives the OCSF ancestry.
---

if $ancestors == null {
  $ancestry = null
} else {
  $ancestry = $ancestors.split("|") if type_of($ancestors).kind == "string" else $ancestors
  $ancestry = $ancestry.where(path => path not in ["", "?", "(truncated)"]).slice(stride=-1)
  $ancestry = $ancestry.map(path => {path: path, name: file_name(path)})
  drop $ancestors
}
